    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1428">

                <pb facs="0939" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg823"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/353.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spanish Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have just received a
                    telegram from the Fathers of San Fernando Cathedral, San Antonio, Texas,
                    informing me that Bishop Segura and Father Vilalta, the last a Spanish subject,
                    have been imprisoned by the Constitutionalists at Tepic.</p>
                <p>I beg to call your attention to the matter and to request your good offices with
                    the Constitutionalists in order to obtain the release of these two priests.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
